WEBVTT

NOTE subtitle = on-screen caption. narrator = Voicebox. They may differ.

title
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<v subtitle>This demo uses AI generated assets.
<v narrator>[narration] introducing Nathan's deep ee-val community nodes.

dt-01-source-1
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:36.099
<v subtitle>Benchmark cases are in a n8n Data Table. The columns are input, expectedOutput, and actualOutput.
<v narrator>[narration] Benchmark cases live in a Data Table with fields such as input, expectedOutput, and the agent’s actualOutput.

dt-01-source-2
00:00:36.741 --> 00:00:51.479
<v subtitle>DeepEval Source is the case store. Trigger will load these rows into the workflow.
<v narrator>[narration] We want our benchmarks cases tested and reported in the dashboard, so we use a Trigger node next.

dt-02-canvas-1
00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:14.137
<v subtitle>Load Source Rows is a Data Table Get. Persist Results is on the canvas and writes to DeepEval Results.
<v narrator>[narration] Nathan builtin Data Table nodes are used to retrieve and store test results.

dt-03-trigger-1
00:01:14.137 --> 00:01:38.072
<v subtitle>DeepEval Trigger is after the Get node. Each table row becomes one eval item with a runId.
<v narrator>[narration] The Trigger node sits after the Get node so each table row becomes one eval item with run identification attached to it.

dt-03-trigger-2
00:01:39.112 --> 00:02:02.005
<v subtitle>The column map fills evalContext from the Data Table fields input, expectedOutput, and actualOutput.
<v narrator>[narration] Column mapping pulls input, expectedOutput, and actualOutput from the Data Table into eval Context.

dt-04-metrics-1
00:02:02.005 --> 00:02:32.328
<v subtitle>G-Eval and Bias are connected to Trigger and score the same case.
<v narrator>[narration] Jee eval and bias metrics connect to the Trigger and score the same loaded case in parallel.

dt-04-metrics-2
00:02:33.705 --> 00:03:05.408
<v subtitle>The local llamafile Chat Model is the judge for both metrics.
<v narrator>[narration] A local Chat Model is the judge for both metrics here, but you can use any Nathan supported model.

dt-05-persist-1
00:03:05.408 --> 00:03:39.444
<v subtitle>Aggregate puts both scores in one row. Persist Results inserts that row into DeepEval Results.
<v narrator>[narration] Aggregate node folds both scores into one row. Persist node inserts that row into deep eval Results data table.

dt-05-persist-2
00:03:40.922 --> 00:04:13.477
<v subtitle>The write is a Data Table Insert. The row has runId, overallScore, overallSuccess, and metrics JSON.

dt-06-execute-1
00:04:13.477 --> 00:04:23.913
<v subtitle>On execute, Get loads a row, Trigger adds a runId, metrics score it, Aggregate emits a row, and Persist writes it.
<v narrator>[narration] Get node reads the source table, the Trigger adds run identification, metrics score it, the Aggregate emits it, and the Persist node writes back.

dt-06-execute-2
00:04:24.566 --> 00:04:38.264
<v subtitle>The local 3B judge is scoring inside the in-process Pyodide pool.
<v narrator>[narration] The local 3 Billion parameter judge is scoring inside the in-process embedded python pool.

dt-06-execute-3
00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:44.787
<v subtitle>G-Eval returns a score, a success flag, and a reason. Persist stores that JSON.
<v narrator>[narration] Jee Eval returns score, success, and a reason, which is what is stored eventually.

dt-07-results-1
00:04:49.133 --> 00:05:18.208
<v subtitle>DeepEval Results has the run that just finished. Persist Results wrote the scores.
<v narrator>[narration] deep ee-val Results now holds the run that just finished.

dt-08-dashboard-1
00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:50.348
<v subtitle>Source cases and result scores are both Data Tables, alongside the dashboard's report PDF.
<v narrator>[narration] Use the dashboard to generate an Agentic Benchmark Checklist report for compliance purposes.
